This was the company's first major acquisition after the one that had failed in Portugal.
Last December, the Montreal company also purchased Peer 1 Network Entreprises, an Internet provider based in Vancouver, for 526 million.
Cogeco revenues grew by 41.5% in the fourth trimester, reaching EUR 504.7 million.
This represents EUR 1.8 billion for the current financial year.
The net profit of its main subsidiary, Cogeco Câble, was EUR 43.9 million, or EUR 90 per share, a decrease from EUR 45.7 million, or EUR 93 per share, of the same period last year.
Cogeco Cable revenues, however, increased by 45 per cent to 47.4 million.
The company lost 15,237 clients in the fourth quarter.
However, for the financial year 2013, Cogeco Câble's clients increased at a rate of 5,546.
Mr Audet does not worry that the number of customers fluctuates in this way.
For me, this is not an indication of a change of trend, he observed.
It varies from one trimester to the next with fierce competition.
Horses in embroidery products
Horse meat has been detected in tin cans of beef products, sold by two low-price UK retailers, the Food Hygiene Agency announced today.
Routine tests revealed that the products, produced in January in Romania and sold by Home Bargains and Quality Save, contained horseDNA of 1 to 5%.
'Because horse meat is not mentioned in the list of ingrtues, it shouldn't have been present in the product,' explained the UK agency.
Scandal about horse-meat in cooked dishes erupted earlier this year, following tests in Ireland.
