Jenny Slate participated in "Saturday Night Live" and was part of the "Walds and Recreation" series, but she is best known for her viral Video series "Marcel The Shell with Shoes On".
Kroll and Slate, as well as other young comedians with a singular voice (the surrealist pessimist Anthony Jeselnik, the ironic defender of racial justice W. Kamau Bell), are pure products of the decentralized American comedy.
