Miscellaneous workers in possession of a 457 visa may have to take an “authenticity” test
The Government was currently studying the possibility of introducing an “authenlity test” for foreign workers in the possession of a 457 visa while it was considering extending law enforcement.
The test, if adopted, would be applied according to a criterion intended to prevent 457 visas from being used for unqualified posts or as a back-to-back means of bringing family and friends to Australia.
A government working document was unveiled today as Labour MP Maxine McKew denounced the government speech on foreign-stretched workers, saying that it could offend Australia's neighbours.
“Shut-whelming statements about 'foreigners returning to queue' and "jobs for Australians first" are unpleasant return at a time when trade unions were asking for a protected labour market," she told the Australia India Institute today.
Historically, this meant that the work of the Whites had to be protected – and I would not be surprised if some countries in the region saw it as an evoking this historical artif artifact.
