If “authenticity” criteria were adopted, a visa applicant could be screened to determine “whether the job offer is genuine in the event that the applicant is a personal relationship or partner of the owner or of the person concerned within the company sponsoring it”.
Firms could also be required to report 457 visa holders after some of them, intending to sponsor a small number of workers, have in fact employed hundreds.
