However, pawn lenders have the advantage of not requesting a verification of creditworthiness or proof of salary, and can unleash loans more quickly than banks.
As a result, millions of people throughout the region are turning to pawned lenders as families feel the pressure exerted by the increase in the cost of living and the over-indebtedness of households and consumers.
After five years of solid growth since the global financial crisis, and low-cost credit backed by too lax monetary policy in advanced economies, low- and middle-middle-income families are turning to pawnbrokers to bridge the difference as their economies are experiencing a slowdown.
