The company will finance them using 60 per cent of the EUR 66 million in Singapore raised this week during its introduction to the Singapore Stock Exchange.
While some lenders at a reduced rate have been criticized for the exorbitant interest rates that they charge, Miss Yeah indicates that praising not only offers lower rates than other lenders, but it does not directly increase the debt.
“Customers mislead property that they already own, monetizing their personal property does not increase household indebtedness,” she says.
Pledging is increasingly being socially accepted as a means of securing guaranteed short-term funding.
Nor are the people who go to pawn lenders alone who have financial problems.
Kneed people from Singapore also go to ValueMax pledging loan shops to pawn gold ingots or Rolex watches, which can account for up to 60 per cent of their cash purchase price.
Customers from all strategies of society.
