Back in black and white for Marie Chouinard, who presents at Danse Danse his two new group choreographies: the first inspired by the inks and poeems of Henri Michaux, the second infused by the sognoliated solos Gymnopédies by Satie.
An unvehicular evening that makes it possible to see Chouinard's prism, from art to tics and from ink black to white.
A white screen serves as a background wall.
On carpet, as white, in the immense space of the Théâtre Maisonneuve, comes forward, in profile, fine like a line and dressed in black, a body.
